# Internal repo files: never serve publicly (briefs go through the
# key-gated /.netlify/functions/brief endpoint instead). Mirrored in
# netlify.toml, which Netlify evaluates first.
/docs/*             /index.html   404!
/scripts/*          /index.html   404!
/data/*             /index.html   404!
/supabase/*         /index.html   404!
/netlify/*          /index.html   404!
/.claude/*          /index.html   404!
/CLAUDE.md          /index.html   404!
/package.json       /index.html   404!
/package-lock.json  /index.html   404!
/DEPLOY-NETLIFY.md  /index.html   404!
/mwinda-netlify.zip /index.html   404!

# A missing asset must 404, not fall through to the SPA catch-all below.
# Without this, a mistyped or not-yet-committed file — assets/hero-platform.mp4,
# say — answers with the whole of index.html at status 200. The browser then
# downloads the entire homepage on every visit while trying to decode it as a
# video, and the real failure is invisible in the network panel because the
# request looks successful.
#
# No "!" on purpose: an unforced rule applies only when no real file matches,
# so every asset that does exist is still served normally.
/assets/*   /index.html   404

/*          /index.html      200
